#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084128} :activity/id #uuid "379bb0b9-1655-5b9e-836d-497f51622d41" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049976 :topic/id #uuid "23404e79-b5c1-5a89-a64b-889c85ed49fa" :topic/math-academy-id 734} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084128 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084452 :tutorial/content "There is a **linear correlation** between two sets of paired observations if the data points on the corresponding scatter plot are located along a straight line.\n\nWe say that the correlation is **positive** if the corresponding trend line has a *positive slope*. Similarly, we say that the correlation is **negative** if the corresponding trend line has a *negative slope*.\n\nWe have a **strong** correlation if the data points lie *close* to the corresponding trend line. Similarly, we have a **weak** correlation if the data points are scattered *far* from the corresponding trend line.\n\nLet's see a few examples:\n\n| ![](images/cd/cdd335fda9e91cbf7cdb05ad18065630985c50adb788df980708d822f7a5e8e9.png) | **Strong positive** linear correlation:\n\n- The trend line has a *positive* slope.\n\n- The data points lie *close* to the trend line. |\n| --- | --- |\n| ![](images/9b/9b288c25fb0993a714768e3e2e9caf23a11f2629950eb03b138acfc0aa6c17cf.png) | **Weak positive** linear correlation: \n\n- The trend line has a *positive* slope.\n\n- The data points lie *far* from the trend line. |\n| ![](images/36/3680700a5e4e4e196db6ffe106535ad784567b9fbed85e5005cbb6e49a476860.png) | **Strong negative** linear correlation:\n\n- The trend line has a *negative* slope.\n\n- The data points lie *close* to the trend line. |\n| ![](images/07/076440b257a78474e9f1b3129ec448a407bb1b49215a29251d8e929cadaeb984.png) | **Weak negative** linear correlation:\n\n- The trend line has a *negative* slope.\n\n- The data points lie *far* from the trend line. |\n| ![](images/ed/ed266d09a86d7200c02f004cd9bb3a87f75693462ff8846f7f3cc1ed4b66ed63.png) | **No linear correlation**:\n\n- The data points are scattered randomly. |" :tutorial/id #uuid "4d19b15d-f5c7-53da-b834-26b49ff2c356" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3698 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "95a44919-d4ba-5d32-a2bd-f69011dce161" :step/math-academy-id 20618 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084290}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084290 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083337 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083139 :question/id #uuid "87541606-5e53-5e3c-aefa-b3d6a6a12961" :question/math-academy-id "e-9696"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef670158-f161-51f8-b146-0c07f8a1fa5d" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050516}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083516} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083517} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545848} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545866} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545874}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Type and Strength of a Given Correlation"} :step/id #uuid "2da7dcd7-da21-537a-8c2e-c0b52615035c" :step/math-academy-id 36348 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084293}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084291 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083338 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083140 :question/id #uuid "8aaa2e17-cd20-5d59-80c5-6ec3c7842672" :question/math-academy-id "e-9697"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b973aca4-f9fc-5b5c-ab75-2329204993ce" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049051}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083518} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083519} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545798} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545811} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545841} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545868}] :knowledge-point/title "Estimating the Correlation Coefficient"} :step/id #uuid "f826ecdd-fef8-5bd8-90d8-82a4bd2eac1f" :step/math-academy-id 36349 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084292}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084292 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083339 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083141 :question/id #uuid "5e64e6c3-80f5-5b23-90fa-8512ad377948" :question/math-academy-id "e-9698"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ebbc6b77-cd04-5509-b344-66feddfed1bb" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083520} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083521} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545794} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545854} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545862} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545878}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Scatter Plot Given a Correlation Coefficient"} :step/id #uuid "93e678b9-6925-580f-85e0-aaf4018c8a15" :step/math-academy-id 36350} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084293 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084490 :tutorial/content "The linear **correlation coefficient** $\\rho$ (the Greek letter rho, pronounced \"row\") is a real number between $-1$ and $1$ that shows the strength of a linear correlation. It has the following properties:\n\n- $\\rho = 1$ indicates a perfect positive correlation\n\n- $\\rho = -1$ indicates a perfect negative correlation\n\n- $\\rho = 0$ indicates no (linear) correlation\n\nThe approximate value of $\\rho$ can be determined from the scatter plot.\n\n| ![](images/09/09d585da995df4e5a67b022816eec246113171d3aad15dcb57d82c766dcb7d18.png) | For a strong positive correlation, we have $0.7 \\leq \\rho \\leq 1.$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| ![](images/9b/9b288c25fb0993a714768e3e2e9caf23a11f2629950eb03b138acfc0aa6c17cf.png) | For a weak positive correlation, we have $0.3 \\leq \\rho \\lt 0.7.$ |\n| ![](images/36/3680700a5e4e4e196db6ffe106535ad784567b9fbed85e5005cbb6e49a476860.png) | For a strong negative correlation, we have $-1 \\leq \\rho \\leq -0.7.$ |\n| ![](images/92/92b65a115fd1621303a248de8ae03d05392827914f5200f267d368867d511ae5.png) | For a weak negative correlation, we have $-0.7 \\lt \\rho \\leq -0.3.$ |\n| ![](images/2c/2cf1e2c3e79940229fc85c10d5bccdfed17afe0759cc897d53e5421328b21466.png) | For little or no correlation, we have $-0.3 < \\rho < 0.3.$ |" :tutorial/id #uuid "c84adf99-1723-5b00-9eb9-b729a194dbe3" :tutorial/math-academy-id 5951 :tutorial/title "The Correlation Coefficient"} :step/id #uuid "40606d75-7f4e-5175-b3e7-b96e62b5b149" :step/math-academy-id 36361 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084291}}] :activity/title "Linear Correlation" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186083427}]}
